{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"a2e5e7fc7a95f2e5","type":"group","x":320,"y":-1080,"width":940,"height":401,"label":"Weaponise"},
		{"id":"f5e971351c2f111d","type":"group","x":320,"y":-11,"width":940,"height":401,"label":"C2"},
		{"id":"db3596128d2b99f1","type":"group","x":-1980,"y":-1080,"width":940,"height":393,"label":"Reconnaissance"},
		{"id":"cfb4a66d1ce4f9e1","type":"group","x":-1980,"y":-30,"width":940,"height":393,"label":"Installation"},
		{"id":"5faea3e0bbec2ca2","type":"group","x":320,"y":-543,"width":940,"height":390,"label":"Delivery"},
		{"id":"eb1fca5dac11b4c4","type":"group","x":-1980,"y":-543,"width":940,"height":390,"label":"Explotation"},
		{"id":"191712a1c8dd1b66","type":"group","x":-860,"y":440,"width":940,"height":360,"label":"Actions on Objectives"},
		{"id":"77f47681e421bb24","type":"text","text":"# Reconnaissance\nResearching the target to find out information.","x":-840,"y":-744,"width":334,"height":134},
		{
			"id":"1513d45e599336fb",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"## Adversary Tactics\nPlan and conduct research:\n- Harvest email address\n- Identify employees on social media\n- Collect all public relations information\n- Discovery internet-facing servers",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1960,
			"y":-1053,
			"width":420,
			"height":341
		},
		{
			"id":"1c19967c11f7c680",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"## SOC Defences\nDiscover adversary's intent:\n- Web log alerts and historical searching data\n- Build playbooks for detecting behaviour that indicate recon activity\n- Prioritise defence around technologies and people that reconnaissance activity is targeting",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1480,
			"y":-1053,
			"width":420,
			"height":341
		},
		{"id":"8b3df30b894a145f","type":"text","text":"# Exploitation\nExecute code on vulnerable system by triggering the code.","x":-840,"y":-410,"width":334,"height":140},
		{
			"id":"d5270d64ab35a1ce",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"## Adversary Tactics\nPrepare and stage the operation:\n- Obtain an automated tool to deliver the malware payload\n- Select or create a document to present to the victim\n- Select or create a backdoor and command and control infrastructure",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":340,
			"y":-1053,
			"width":420,
			"height":347
		},
		{
			"id":"c46a14fca67d138a",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"## SOC Defences\nTrain employees, secure code and harden devices:\n- Employee security awareness training and periodic email testing\n- Web developer training for securing code\n- Regular vulnerability scanning and penetration testing\n- Endpoint hardening measures\n- Endpoint auditing to forensically determine origin of exploit",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1480,
			"y":-517,
			"width":420,
			"height":341
		},
		{
			"id":"81cfbae32c999962",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"## Adversary Tactics\nExploit a vulnerability to gain access:\n- Use software, hardware or human vulnerability\n- Acquire or develop the exploit\n- Use an adversary-triggered exploit for server vulnerabilities\n- Use a victim-triggered exploit such as opening an email attachment",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1960,
			"y":-517,
			"width":420,
			"height":341
		},
		{"id":"d9ff3dd155bb0ec7","type":"text","text":"# Weaponisation\nPairing remote malware to create a paylaod.","x":-280,"y":-750,"width":334,"height":146},
		{"id":"d22eed8e75e0a4fc","type":"text","text":"# Installation\nInstallation of backdoor on target to install malware and obtain persistance.","x":-850,"y":-100,"width":354,"height":140},
		{
			"id":"71aca3b06ace4746",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"## Adversary Tactics\nInstall persistent backdoor:\n- Install web shell on web server for persistent access\n- Create point of persistence by adding services, autorun keys etc\n- Some adversaries modify the timestamp of the malware to make it appear as part of the OS",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1960,
			"y":-4,
			"width":420,
			"height":341
		},
		{
			"id":"57321bd7b3b28f28",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"## SOC Defences\nDetect, log and analyse installation activity:\n- HIPS to alert or block common installation paths\n- Determine if malware requires elevated privileges or user privileges\n- Endpoint auditing to discover abnormal file creations\n- Determine if malware is known threat or new variant",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1480,
			"y":-4,
			"width":420,
			"height":341
		},
		{
			"id":"d17bf600d0e91381",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"## Adversary Tactics\nReap the rewards of successful attack:\n- Collect user credentials\n- Privilege escalation\n- Internal reconnaissance\n- Lateral movement through environment\n- Collect and exfiltrate data\n- Destroy systems\n- Overwrite, modify or corrupt data",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-840,
			"y":460,
			"width":420,
			"height":320
		},
		{
			"id":"bd7bd4caeabeb15d",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"## SOC Defences\nDetect by using forensic evidence:\n- Establish incident response playbook\n- Detect data exfiltration, lateral movement and unauthorised credential usage\n- Immediate analyst response for all alerts\n- Forensic analysis of endpoints for rapid triage\n- Network packet captures to recreate activity\n- Conduct damage assessment",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-360,
			"y":460,
			"width":420,
			"height":320
		},
		{"id":"1d522ed3881e1c07","type":"text","text":"# Actions on Objectives \nExecute actions to reach their goal.","x":-580,"y":200,"width":374,"height":120},
		{
			"id":"56267aa0072230b7",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"## SOC Defences\nDetect and collect weaponisation artifacts:\n- Ensure that IDS rules and signatures are up to date\n- Conduct full malware analysis\n- Build detections for the behaviour of known weaponisers\n- Collect files and metadata for future analysis",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":820,
			"y":-1053,
			"width":420,
			"height":347
		},
		{"id":"94af40e263e1f9cc","type":"text","text":"# Delivery\nDelivering weapon to victim through email or other means.","x":-280,"y":-410,"width":334,"height":140},
		{"id":"3e46cf0d34735ab7","type":"text","text":"# Command & Control (C2)\nOutside server command channel is created to manipulate target.","x":-280,"y":-100,"width":354,"height":140},
		{
			"id":"1d27e311fcf61b5b",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"## Adversary Tactics\nOpen channel for targeted manipulation:\n- Open two-way communication channel to CNC infrastructure\n- Most common CNC channels over web, DNS and email protocols\n- CNC infrastructure may be adversary owned or another victim network itself",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":340,
			"y":16,
			"width":420,
			"height":347
		},
		{
			"id":"54d8097e5bb8d4f3",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"## SOC Defences\nLast chance to block operation:\n- Research possible new CNC infrastructures \n- Discover CNC infrastructure through malware analysis\n- Isolate DNS traffic to suspect DNS servers, especially Dynamic DNS\n- Blocking or disable CNC channel\n- Consolidate the number of internet points of presence\n- Customise rules blocking of CNC protocols on web proxies",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":820,
			"y":16,
			"width":420,
			"height":347
		},
		{
			"id":"8480d65f186dd578",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"## Adversary Tactics\nLaunch malware at target:\n- Direct against web servers\n- Indirect delivery through\n\t- Malicious email\n\t- Malware on USB\n\t- Social media interactions",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":340,
			"y":-517,
			"width":420,
			"height":347
		},
		{
			"id":"329cf88fad1dc4ef",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"## SOC Defences\nBlock delivery of malware:\n- Analyse the infrastructure path used for delivery\n- Understand targeted servers, people and data available to attack\n- Infer intent of the adversary based on targeting\n- Collect email and web logs for forensic reconstruction",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":820,
			"y":-517,
			"width":420,
			"height":341
		}
	],
